course: dictionary
lesson: 12811
title: Elongated: longer than usual
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Elongated means longer and thinner than usual, as if something has been stretched out. «The eel had an elongated body that slid through the water.» The eel is not just long: its body is long and thin in a way that a fish or a ball is not. The word is the clue to its shape.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. «The leaves were elongated, much longer than they were wide.» The words longer than they were wide tell you what elongated means. A good check is to swap in a simpler word, such as long and thin, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word also appears in art and maths. An oval is an elongated circle, because it is stretched out, longer in one direction than the other. «At sunset, the shadows were elongated across the grass.» The sun is low, so the shadows stretch out long.
fact: Elongated means longer and thinner than usual; stretched out.
fact: «Elongated» is an adjective, so it describes a thing, like «an elongated body» or «elongated leaves».
fact: Elongate is the verb, meaning to make something longer. The past form is elongated.
fact: An oval is an elongated circle: it is stretched out, not perfectly round.
fact: In the evening, when the sun is low, shadows can look elongated because they stretch far across the ground.
exercise: «The eel had an elongated body.» What does elongated mean? | Very heavy | Short and round | *Longer and thinner than usual | Bright and shiny
exercise: Mia says an oval is an elongated circle. What does she mean? | Exactly the same as a circle | A circle with a hole in the middle | *Stretched out, longer in one direction than a normal circle | A smaller circle
exercise: «At sunset, the shadows were elongated across the grass.» Find and copy one word from the sentence that means long and thin. | sunset | *elongated | across | grass
exercise: Which description fits the word elongated best? | A tiny dot | A round, bouncy ball | *A long, thin pencil | A small, fat pebble
test: «The worm's elongated body wriggled into the soil.» What does this tell you about the worm? | Its body was short and fat | *Its body was long and thin | It could fly | It was made of metal
test: Ben draws an elongated oval. What shape is it? | *A circle stretched out, longer than it is wide | A square | A perfect circle | A triangle
exam: Which sentence uses elongated correctly? | *Her elongated fingers reached the top shelf easily | The sun was elongated at noon, a perfect circle | The cake was elongated and round like a ball | The puddle was elongated and very deep, like a bowl
